IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc17-dna-samples.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 487.056 to 487.0911: when and how DNA samples are taken, the report, the
-- immunity of the officer, the investigative procedures, the duty to inform, verification against the data bank, the use of the substances and results, their
-- destruction, additional samples, and review by the Attorney General. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Same conventions as ccc17-dna-orders.l4.
-- A duty ("shall") is encoded as "the section imposes the duty on these facts": JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the text's own "if", "unless" or "where" fails
-- (marginal reading (a)); NOTHING where the person or case lies outside the words used. A grant ("may") whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (fork F1).

§ `Section 487.056 -- When collection is to take place; who collects`

DECLARE `s 487.056 time for taking the samples` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.056(1)(a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
    `s 487.056(1)(b) on the day on which the order authorizing the taking of the samples is made or as soon as feasible afterwards`
    `s 487.056(2)(a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11) or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
    `s 487.056(2)(b) as soon as feasible after the authorization is granted`
    `s 487.056(3)(a) when the person is arrested under a warrant issued under subsection 487.0551(1) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
    `s 487.056(3)(b) as soon as feasible after the person appears at the place set out in the order or summons`

-- covers: 487.056(1), 487.056(1)(a), 487.056(1)(b)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person subject to the order > power
-- src:9639 | 487.056 (1) Samples of bodily substances shall be taken as authorized under section 487.051
-- src:9640 | (a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or as soon as feasible afterwards; or
-- src:9641 | (b) in any other case, on the day on which the order authorizing the taking of the samples is made or as soon as feasible afterwards.
@ref s 487.056(1) (src:9639-9641)
-- "as soon as feasible" is an undefined period: the text gives no number of days, so no deadline is computed.
GIVEN `the samples are to be taken as authorized under section 487.051` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order was made under subsection 487.051(4) setting out a place, day and time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 487.056 time for taking the samples`
`s 487.056(1) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.051` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the samples are to be taken as authorized under section 487.051` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `an order was made under subsection 487.051(4) setting out a place, day and time` THEN JUST `s 487.056(1)(a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 487.056(1)(b) on the day on which the order authorizing the taking of the samples is made or as soon as feasible afterwards`

-- covers: 487.056(2), 487.056(2)(a), 487.056(2)(b)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person subject to the authorization > power
-- src:9643 | (2) Samples of bodily substances shall be taken as authorized under section 487.055 or 487.091
-- src:9644 | (a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11) or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) or as soon as feasible afterwards; or
-- src:9645 | (b) in any other case, as soon as feasible after the authorization is granted.
@ref s 487.056(2) (src:9643-9645)
GIVEN `the samples are to be taken as authorized under section 487.055 or 487.091` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order was made under subsection 487.055(3.11), or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) was directed to the person, setting out a place, day and time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 487.056 time for taking the samples`
`s 487.056(2) the time at which the samples shall be taken under section 487.055 or 487.091` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the samples are to be taken as authorized under section 487.055 or 487.091` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `an order was made under subsection 487.055(3.11), or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) was directed to the person, setting out a place, day and time` THEN JUST `s 487.056(2)(a) at the place, day and time set out in an order made under subsection 487.055(3.11) or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 487.056(2)(b) as soon as feasible after the authorization is granted`

-- covers: 487.056(3), 487.056(3)(a), 487.056(3)(b)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person who failed to appear > power
-- src:9647 | (3) If a person fails to appear as required by an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3), samples of bodily substances shall be taken
-- src:9648 | (a) when the person is arrested under a warrant issued under subsection 487.0551(1) or as soon as feasible afterwards; or
-- src:9649 | (b) as soon as feasible after the person appears at the place set out in the order or summons if no warrant is issued.
@ref s 487.056(3) (src:9647-9649)
GIVEN `the person fails to appear as required by an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant has been issued under subsection 487.0551(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 487.056 time for taking the samples`
`s 487.056(3) the time at which the samples shall be taken when the person fails to appear` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person fails to appear as required by an order made under subsection 487.051(4) or 487.055(3.11) or a summons referred to in subsection 487.055(4) or 487.091(3)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `a warrant has been issued under subsection 487.0551(1)` THEN JUST `s 487.056(3)(a) when the person is arrested under a warrant issued under subsection 487.0551(1) or as soon as feasible afterwards`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 487.056(3)(b) as soon as feasible after the person appears at the place set out in the order or summons`

-- covers: 487.056(4)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > a peace officer > no-right
-- src:9651 | (4) Subsections (1) to (3) apply even if the order or authorization to take the samples of bodily substances is appealed.
@ref s 487.056(4) (src:9651)
GIVEN `the order or authorization to take the samples of bodily substances is appealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.056(4) subsections (1) to (3) apply even though the order or authorization is appealed` MEANS
    IF `the order or authorization to take the samples of bodily substances is appealed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

-- covers: 487.056(5)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person subject to the order or authorization > power
-- src:9653 | (5) A peace officer who is authorized under section 487.051, 487.055 or 487.091 to take samples of bodily substances may cause the samples to be taken in any place in Canada in which the person who is subject to the order or authorization is located.
@ref s 487.056(5) (src:9653)
GIVEN `the peace officer is authorized under section 487.051, 487.055 or 487.091 to take samples of bodily substances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who is subject to the order or authorization is located in that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.056(5) the peace officer may cause the samples to be taken in the place` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer is authorized under section 487.051, 487.055 or 487.091 to take samples of bodily substances` AND `the place is in Canada` AND `the person who is subject to the order or authorization is located in that place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

DECLARE `s 487.056(6) who takes the samples` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.056(6) a peace officer`
    `s 487.056(6) a person acting under the direction of a peace officer`
    `s 487.056(6) someone else`

-- covers: 487.056(6)
-- fork: F4
-- jural: the person subject to the order or authorization > the person who takes the samples > right
-- src:9655 | (6) The samples shall be taken by a peace officer who has jurisdiction over the person or in the place in which the samples are taken — or a person acting under their direction — who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take them.
@ref s 487.056(6) (src:9655)
-- Reading taken (fork F4): the peace officer who takes the samples, or who directs the person taking them, must have jurisdiction over the person or in the place,
-- and whoever actually takes them must be able, by virtue of training or experience, to do so.
GIVEN taker IS A `s 487.056(6) who takes the samples`
      `the peace officer who takes the samples, or who directs the person taking them, has jurisdiction over the person or in the place in which the samples are taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who takes the samples is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.056(6) the samples are taken by a person the subsection permits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF taker EQUALS `s 487.056(6) someone else` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The samples shall be taken by a peace officer who has jurisdiction over the person or in the place in which the samples are taken — or a person acting under their direction"
        IF NOT `the peace officer who takes the samples, or who directs the person taking them, has jurisdiction over the person or in the place in which the samples are taken` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a peace officer who has jurisdiction over the person or in the place in which the samples are taken"
        IF NOT `the person who takes the samples is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take them` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who is able, by virtue of training or experience, to take them"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.057 -- Report of peace officer`

DECLARE `s 487.057(1) instrument under which the samples were taken` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.057(1) a warrant under section 487.05`
    `s 487.057(1) an authorization under section 487.055`
    `s 487.057(1) an authorization under section 487.091`
    `s 487.057(1) an order under section 487.051`
    `s 487.057(1) another instrument`

DECLARE `s 487.057(1) where the report is filed` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.057(1)(a) with the provincial court judge who issued the warrant or granted the authorization, or another judge of that provincial court`
    `s 487.057(1)(b) with the court that made the order under section 487.051`

-- covers: 487.057(1), 487.057(1)(a), 487.057(1)(b)
-- jural: the court that issued the instrument > a peace officer > right
-- src:9657 | 487.057 (1) A peace officer who takes samples of bodily substances from a person or who causes a person who is not a peace officer to take samples under their direction shall, as soon as feasible after the samples are taken, make a written report in Form 5.07 and cause the report to be filed with
-- src:9658 | (a) the provincial court judge who issued the warrant under section 487.05 or granted the authorization under section 487.055 or 487.091 or another judge of that provincial court; or
-- src:9659 | (b) the court that made the order under section 487.051.
@ref s 487.057(1) (src:9657-9659)
-- "as soon as feasible": undefined period, no deadline invented. The duty is on a peace officer who takes samples or causes a person who is not a peace officer to take
-- them under their direction; the second function says with whom the report is filed.
GIVEN `the peace officer takes samples of bodily substances from a person or causes a person who is not a peace officer to take samples under their direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.057(1) the peace officer shall make a written report in Form 5.07 and cause it to be filed` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer takes samples of bodily substances from a person or causes a person who is not a peace officer to take samples under their direction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

@ref s 487.057(1) (where filed) (src:9657-9659)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 487.057(1) instrument under which the samples were taken`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 487.057(1) where the report is filed`
`s 487.057(1) with whom the report shall be filed` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `s 487.057(1) a warrant under section 487.05` THEN JUST `s 487.057(1)(a) with the provincial court judge who issued the warrant or granted the authorization, or another judge of that provincial court`
    WHEN `s 487.057(1) an authorization under section 487.055` THEN JUST `s 487.057(1)(a) with the provincial court judge who issued the warrant or granted the authorization, or another judge of that provincial court`
    WHEN `s 487.057(1) an authorization under section 487.091` THEN JUST `s 487.057(1)(a) with the provincial court judge who issued the warrant or granted the authorization, or another judge of that provincial court`
    WHEN `s 487.057(1) an order under section 487.051` THEN JUST `s 487.057(1)(b) with the court that made the order under section 487.051`
    WHEN `s 487.057(1) another instrument` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

DECLARE `s 487.057(2) matter in the report` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.057(2)(a) a statement of the time and date the samples were taken`
    `s 487.057(2)(b) a description of the bodily substances that were taken`
    `s 487.057(2) another matter`

-- covers: 487.057(2)
-- jural: the court that receives the report > a peace officer > right
-- src:9661 | (2) The report shall include
-- src:9662 | (a) a statement of the time and date the samples were taken; and
-- src:9663 | (b) a description of the bodily substances that were taken.
@ref s 487.057(2) (src:9661-9663)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 487.057(2) matter in the report`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.057(2) the report shall include the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 487.057(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 487.057(3)
-- jural: a peace officer who requested the taking > a peace officer who took the samples > right
-- src:9665 | (3) A peace officer who takes the samples or causes the samples to be taken under their direction at the request of another peace officer shall send a copy of the report to the other peace officer unless that other peace officer had jurisdiction to take the samples.
@ref s 487.057(3) (src:9665)
GIVEN `the peace officer takes the samples, or causes them to be taken under their direction, at the request of another peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other peace officer had jurisdiction to take the samples` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.057(3) the peace officer shall send a copy of the report to the other peace officer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the peace officer takes the samples, or causes them to be taken under their direction, at the request of another peace officer` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the other peace officer had jurisdiction to take the samples` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless that other peace officer had jurisdiction to take the samples"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.058 -- No criminal or civil liability`

DECLARE `s 487.058 who acts` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.058 a peace officer`
    `s 487.058 a person acting under a peace officer’s direction`
    `s 487.058 someone else`

-- covers: 487.058
-- jural: a peace officer or a person acting under a peace officer’s direction > the person from whom the samples were taken > immunity
-- src:9667 | 487.058 No peace officer, and no person acting under a peace officer’s direction, incurs any criminal or civil liability for anything necessarily done with reasonable care and skill in the taking of samples of bodily substances from a person under a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091.
@ref s 487.058 (src:9667)
-- "No peace officer ... incurs any criminal or civil liability for anything necessarily done with reasonable care and skill in the taking of samples ... under a warrant,
-- order or authorization": the immunity is limited by its own wording, so a case outside it is NOTHING (the section does not say that liability follows).
GIVEN actor IS A `s 487.058 who acts`
      `the thing was necessarily done with reasonable care and skill in the taking of samples of bodily substances from a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the samples were taken under a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.058 the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF actor EQUALS `s 487.058 someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the thing was necessarily done with reasonable care and skill in the taking of samples of bodily substances from a person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the samples were taken under a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.06 -- Investigative procedures`

DECLARE `s 487.06(1) means of taking samples` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.06(1)(a) the plucking of individual hairs from the person, including the root sheath`
    `s 487.06(1)(b) the taking of buccal swabs by swabbing the lips, tongue and inside cheeks of the mouth to collect epithelial cells`
    `s 487.06(1)(c) the taking of blood by pricking the skin surface with a sterile lancet`
    `s 487.06(1) another means`

-- covers: 487.06(1), 487.06(1)(a), 487.06(1)(b), 487.06(1)(c)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person from whom the samples are taken > power
-- src:9669 | 487.06 (1) A peace officer or a person acting under a peace officer’s direction is authorized by a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091 to take samples of bodily substances by any of the following means:
-- src:9670 | (a) the plucking of individual hairs from the person, including the root sheath;
-- src:9671 | (b) the taking of buccal swabs by swabbing the lips, tongue and inside cheeks of the mouth to collect epithelial cells; or
-- src:9672 | (c) the taking of blood by pricking the skin surface with a sterile lancet.
@ref s 487.06(1) (src:9669-9672)
GIVEN means IS A `s 487.06(1) means of taking samples`
      `the peace officer, or the person acting under the peace officer’s direction, acts under a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.06(1) the means is one by which the peace officer is authorized to take samples of bodily substances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the peace officer, or the person acting under the peace officer’s direction, acts under a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF means EQUALS `s 487.06(1) another means` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 487.06(2)
-- jural: the person from whom the samples are taken > the provincial court judge or court > right
-- src:9674 | (2) The warrant, order or authorization shall include any terms and conditions that the provincial court judge or court, as the case may be, considers advisable to ensure that the taking of the samples authorized by the warrant, order or authorization is reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 487.06(2) (src:9674)
GIVEN `the provincial court judge or court considers the term or condition advisable to ensure that the taking of the samples authorized is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.06(2) the warrant, order or authorization shall include the term or condition` MEANS
    IF `the provincial court judge or court considers the term or condition advisable to ensure that the taking of the samples authorized is reasonable in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

DECLARE `s 487.06(3) instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.06(3) an order made under section 487.051`
    `s 487.06(3) an authorization granted under section 487.055`
    `s 487.06(3) an authorization granted under section 487.091`
    `s 487.06(3) a warrant issued under section 487.05`
    `s 487.06(3) another instrument`

-- covers: 487.06(3)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person from whom the samples are taken > power
-- src:9676 | (3) A peace officer who is authorized to take samples of bodily substances from a person by an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091, or a person acting under their direction, may take fingerprints from the person for the purpose of the DNA Identification Act.
@ref s 487.06(3) (src:9676)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 487.06(3) instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.06(3) the peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, may take fingerprints from the person for the purpose of the DNA Identification Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `s 487.06(3) an order made under section 487.051` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 487.06(3) an authorization granted under section 487.055` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 487.06(3) an authorization granted under section 487.091` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 487.06(3) a warrant issued under section 487.05` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
    WHEN `s 487.06(3) another instrument` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§ `Section 487.07 -- Duty to inform, detention, privacy, rights of a young person`

DECLARE `s 487.07(1) matter to be told` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.07(1)(a) the contents of the warrant, order or authorization`
    `s 487.07(1)(b) the nature of the investigative procedures by means of which the samples are to be taken`
    `s 487.07(1)(c) the purpose of taking the samples`
    `s 487.07(1)(d) the authority of the peace officer and any other person under the direction of the peace officer to use as much force as is necessary for the purpose of taking the samples`
    `s 487.07(1)(e)(i) the possibility that the results of forensic DNA analysis may be used in evidence`
    `s 487.07(1)(e)(ii) the rights of the young person under subsection (4)`

-- covers: 487.07(1), 487.07(1)(a), 487.07(1)(b), 487.07(1)(c), 487.07(1)(d), 487.07(1)(e)
-- jural: the person from whom the samples are to be taken > a peace officer > right
-- src:9678 | 487.07 (1) Before taking samples of bodily substances from a person, or causing samples to be taken under their direction, in execution of a warrant issued under section 487.05 or an order made under section 487.051 or under an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091, a peace officer shall inform the person of
-- src:9679 | (a) the contents of the warrant, order or authorization;
-- src:9680 | (b) the nature of the investigative procedures by means of which the samples are to be taken;
-- src:9681 | (c) the purpose of taking the samples;
-- src:9682 | (d) the authority of the peace officer and any other person under the direction of the peace officer to use as much force as is necessary for the purpose of taking the samples; and
-- src:9683 | (d.1) [Repealed, 2000, c. 10, s. 20]
-- src:9684 | (e) in the case of samples of bodily substances taken in execution of a warrant,
-- src:9685 | (i) the possibility that the results of forensic DNA analysis may be used in evidence, and
-- src:9686 | (ii) if the sample is taken from a young person, the rights of the young person under subsection (4).
@ref s 487.07(1) (src:9678-9686)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 487.07(1) matter to be told`
      `the peace officer is about to take samples, or cause them to be taken, in execution of a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the samples are taken in execution of a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sample is taken from a young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.07(1) the peace officer shall inform the person of the matter before taking the samples` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the peace officer is about to take samples, or cause them to be taken, in execution of a warrant issued under section 487.05, an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF matter EQUALS `s 487.07(1)(a) the contents of the warrant, order or authorization` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF matter EQUALS `s 487.07(1)(b) the nature of the investigative procedures by means of which the samples are to be taken` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF matter EQUALS `s 487.07(1)(c) the purpose of taking the samples` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF matter EQUALS `s 487.07(1)(d) the authority of the peace officer and any other person under the direction of the peace officer to use as much force as is necessary for the purpose of taking the samples` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the samples are taken in execution of a warrant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF matter EQUALS `s 487.07(1)(e)(i) the possibility that the results of forensic DNA analysis may be used in evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the sample is taken from a young person` THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (e)(ii): the rights of the young person under subsection (4)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the sample is taken from a young person, the rights of the young person under subsection (4)"

-- covers: 487.07(2), 487.07(2)(a)
-- jural: a peace officer > the person from whom the samples are to be taken > power
-- src:9688 | (2) A person from whom samples of bodily substances are to be taken may
-- src:9689 | (a) be detained for that purpose for a period that is reasonable in the circumstances; and
-- src:9690 | (b) be required to accompany a peace officer for that purpose.
