§ `Section 487.071 -- Verification against the national DNA data bank`

-- covers: 487.071(1)
-- jural: the person subject to the order or authorization > a peace officer > right
-- src:9703 | 487.071 (1) Before taking samples of bodily substances from a person under an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.055 or 487.091, a peace officer, or a person acting under their direction, shall verify whether the convicted offenders index of the national DNA data bank, established under the DNA Identification Act, contains the person’s DNA profile.
