§ `Section 487.09 -- Destruction of bodily substances and results`

DECLARE `s 487.09(1) ground for destruction` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.09(1)(a) the results of the analysis establish that the bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b) was not from that person`
    `s 487.09(1)(b) the person is finally acquitted of the designated offence and any other offence in respect of the same transaction`
    `s 487.09(1)(c)(i) one year after the person is discharged after a preliminary inquiry into the designated offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction`
    `s 487.09(1)(c)(ii) one year after the dismissal, for any reason other than acquittal, or the withdrawal of any information charging the person`
    `s 487.09(1)(c)(iii) one year after any proceeding against the person for the offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction is stayed under section 579 or under that section as applied by section 572 or 795`
    `s 487.09(1) none of those`

-- covers: 487.09(1), 487.09(1)(a), 487.09(1)(b), 487.09(1)(c), 487.09(1) closing words
-- fork: F5
-- jural: the person from whom the substances were taken > the person who holds them > right
-- src:9728 | 487.09 (1) Subject to subsection (2), bodily substances that are taken from a person in execution of a warrant under section 487.05 and the results of forensic DNA analysis shall be destroyed or, in the case of results in electronic form, access to those results shall be permanently removed, without delay after
-- src:9729 | (a) the results of that analysis establish that the bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b) was not from that person;
-- src:9730 | (b) the person is finally acquitted of the designated offence and any other offence in respect of the same transaction; or
-- src:9731 | (c) the expiration of one year after
-- src:9732 | (i) the person is discharged after a preliminary inquiry into the designated offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction,
-- src:9733 | (ii) the dismissal, for any reason other than acquittal, or the withdrawal of any information charging the person with the designated offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction, or
-- src:9734 | (iii) any proceeding against the person for the offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction is stayed under section 579 or under that section as applied by section 572 or 795,
-- src:9735 | unless during that year a new information is laid or an indictment is preferred charging the person with the designated offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction or the proceeding is recommenced.
@ref s 487.09(1) (src:9728-9735)
-- "Subject to subsection (2)": an order under (2) not to destroy suspends the duty (JUST FALSE). Paragraph (c): the duty arises on the expiration of one year after the event
-- and not at all if a new information is laid, an indictment is preferred or the proceeding is recommenced during that year ("unless": JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `the bodily substances were taken from the person in execution of a warrant under section 487.05` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order under subsection (2) that they not be destroyed is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `s 487.09(1) ground for destruction`
      `one year has expired since that event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `during that year a new information is laid or an indictment is preferred charging the person with the designated offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction, or the proceeding is recommenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.09(1) the bodily substances and the results of forensic DNA analysis shall be destroyed without delay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the bodily substances were taken from the person in execution of a warrant under section 487.05` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `an order under subsection (2) that they not be destroyed is in force` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (2)"
        IF ground EQUALS `s 487.09(1)(a) the results of the analysis establish that the bodily substance referred to in paragraph 487.05(1)(b) was not from that person` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF ground EQUALS `s 487.09(1)(b) the person is finally acquitted of the designated offence and any other offence in respect of the same transaction` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF ground EQUALS `s 487.09(1) none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)
        IF NOT `one year has expired since that event` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the expiration of one year after"
        IF `during that year a new information is laid or an indictment is preferred charging the person with the designated offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction, or the proceeding is recommenced` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless during that year a new information is laid or an indictment is preferred charging the person with the designated offence or any other offence in respect of the same transaction or the proceeding is recommenced"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The one year of paragraph (c): the year expires on the anniversary of the event (fork F5: the text has no rule for counting the day; the Interpretation Act is not among the sources).
-- fork: F5
@ref s 487.09(1)(c) (the year) (src:9731-9735)
GIVEN `the day of the discharge, the dismissal or withdrawal, or the stay of proceedings` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 487.09(1)(c) the day on which one year after the event expires` MEANS
    `add years` `the day of the discharge, the dismissal or withdrawal, or the stay of proceedings` 1

GIVEN `the day of the discharge, the dismissal or withdrawal, or the stay of proceedings` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.09(1)(c) one year after the event has expired on the day in question` MEANS
    `the day in question` GREATER THAN `s 487.09(1)(c) the day on which one year after the event expires` `the day of the discharge, the dismissal or withdrawal, or the stay of proceedings`

-- covers: 487.09(2)
