-- covers: 487.091(3)
-- jural: the person not in custody > the court > liability
-- src:9747 | (3) If the court authorizes the taking of samples of bodily substances from a person who is not in custody, a summons in Form 5.061 setting out the information referred to in paragraphs 487.07(1)(b) to (d) shall be directed to the person requiring them to report at the place, day and time set out in the summons and submit to the taking of the samples. Subsections 487.055(5) and (6) apply, with any modifications that the circumstances require.
@ref s 487.091(3) (src:9747)
-- The reference to subsection 487.055(6) is to a subsection this text shows repealed (finding in NOTES.md); the rule of incorporation is encoded for subsection (5) only.
GIVEN `the court authorizes the taking of samples of bodily substances from a person who is not in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.091(3) a summons in Form 5.061 shall be directed to the person requiring them to report and submit to the taking of the samples` MEANS
    IF `the court authorizes the taking of samples of bodily substances from a person who is not in custody`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court authorizes the taking of samples of bodily substances from a person who is not in custody"

@ref s 487.091(3) (incorporation) (src:9747)
GIVEN `a summons in Form 5.061 is directed to the person under subsection 487.091(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.091(3) subsection 487.055(5) applies to the summons with the modifications that the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF `a summons in Form 5.061 is directed to the person under subsection 487.091(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§ `Section 487.0911 -- Review by Attorney General`

DECLARE `s 487.0911 opinion of the Attorney General` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.0911 the defect is due to a clerical error`
    `s 487.0911 the offence referred to in the order or authorization is not a designated offence`
    `s 487.0911 the offence referred to in the order or authorization is a designated offence`

-- covers: 487.0911(1)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the Attorney General > right
-- src:9749 | 487.0911 (1) On receipt of a notice from the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police under subsection 5.2(1) of the DNA Identification Act that an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.091 appears to be defective, the Attorney General shall review the order or authorization and the court record.
@ref s 487.0911(1) (src:9749)
GIVEN `the Attorney General receives a notice from the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police under subsection 5.2(1) of the DNA Identification Act that an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.091 appears to be defective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0911(1) the Attorney General shall review the order or authorization and the court record` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General receives a notice from the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police under subsection 5.2(1) of the DNA Identification Act that an order made under section 487.051 or an authorization granted under section 487.091 appears to be defective`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.0911(2), 487.0911(2)(a), 487.0911(2)(b)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the Attorney General > liability
-- src:9751 | (2) If the Attorney General is of the opinion that the defect is due to a clerical error, the Attorney General shall
-- src:9752 | (a) apply, ex parte, to the judge who made the order or authorization, or to a judge of the same court, to have it corrected; and
-- src:9753 | (b) transmit a copy of the corrected order or authorization, if any, to the Commissioner.
@ref s 487.0911(2) (src:9751-9753)
GIVEN opinion IS A `s 487.0911 opinion of the Attorney General`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0911(2) the Attorney General shall apply ex parte to have the order or authorization corrected` MEANS
    IF opinion EQUALS `s 487.0911 the defect is due to a clerical error`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Attorney General is of the opinion that the defect is due to a clerical error"

@ref s 487.0911(2)(b) (src:9751-9753)
GIVEN opinion IS A `s 487.0911 opinion of the Attorney General`
      `a corrected order or authorization is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0911(2)(b) the Attorney General shall transmit a copy of the corrected order or authorization to the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF opinion EQUALS `s 487.0911 the defect is due to a clerical error` AND `a corrected order or authorization is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "transmit a copy of the corrected order or authorization, if any"

-- covers: 487.0911(3)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the Attorney General > liability
-- src:9755 | (3) If the Attorney General is of the opinion that the offence referred to in the order or authorization is not a designated offence, the Attorney General shall inform the Commissioner of that opinion.
@ref s 487.0911(3) (src:9755)
GIVEN opinion IS A `s 487.0911 opinion of the Attorney General`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0911(3) the Attorney General shall inform the Commissioner of the opinion that the offence is not a designated offence` MEANS
    IF opinion EQUALS `s 487.0911 the offence referred to in the order or authorization is not a designated offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Attorney General is of the opinion that the offence referred to in the order or authorization is not a designated offence"

-- covers: 487.0911(4)
-- jural: the person subject to the order > the Attorney General > liability
-- src:9757 | (4) If the Attorney General is of the opinion that the offence referred to in the order or authorization is a designated offence, the Attorney General shall transmit that opinion, with written reasons, to the Commissioner.
@ref s 487.0911(4) (src:9757)
GIVEN opinion IS A `s 487.0911 opinion of the Attorney General`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0911(4) the Attorney General shall transmit the opinion, with written reasons, to the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF opinion EQUALS `s 487.0911 the offence referred to in the order or authorization is a designated offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Attorney General is of the opinion that the offence referred to in the order or authorization is a designated offence"
